From 0c589c9c4341ddc4150ee781086c9cce7dc8b13a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 04:46:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ladspa: stop and join the worker when the plugin is dropped

The worker's loop had no way out, and DfPlugin kept the worker's
JoinHandle only to drop it, which detaches the thread. So every instance
a host destroyed left its worker polling the input queue every half
millisecond, with its model in memory, for the rest of the host's life,
and still running this library's code if the host unloaded it, as
EasyEffects does when it destroys its LADSPA wrapper. EasyEffects stopped
destroying this plugin's instances on unlink for that reason (issue
#4652), but a preset without the plugin, or a change of model, still
destroys one.

Now the worker checks a flag once a turn of its loop, and Drop sets the
flag and joins the worker, so cleanup() returns with the thread gone. It
waits at most one poll sleep, or the frame being processed.

The new test is a binary of its own, so nothing else starts or ends a
thread while it counts /proc/self/task. It makes and drops a mono and a
stereo plugin three times each, after a first, and without this change it
fails on the first round.

Measured with a C host that instantiated, activated, deactivated and
cleaned up the stereo plugin five times without a run(). Unpatched, it
ended with six threads, 130 MB resident and 0.28 s of CPU over two idle
seconds, where it began with one thread and 4 MB. Patched, it ended with
one thread, 27 MB and no CPU.
